  "scenario": "You are deploying a backend application that needs to upload backup logs to a storage bucket.\n\n1.  **Security Requirement:** The application must have Full Control over one specific S3 bucket.\n2.  **Constraint:** You are strictly forbidden from storing AWS Access Keys or Secret Keys on the server's disk.\n3.  **Solution:** You must create an IAM Role with a custom policy and assign it to the EC2 instance.\n\nAs the Cloud Engineer, you must:\n\n1.  Create the **S3 Bucket**.\n2.  Create a strict **IAM Policy** (Permissions).\n3.  Create an **IAM Role** (Identity) and attach the policy.\n4.  Launch an **EC2 Instance** with the role attached.\n5.  **Verify** access by uploading a file via the command line.\n\n---",
